  "examples": [
    {
      "coptic": "ⲁⲗⲗⲁ ⲡ**ϣⲱⲗⲙ** ⲟⲛ ⲉϥϣⲁⲛϩⲩⲇⲁⲛⲉ ⲛⲥⲁⲡⲉⲥⲧⲟⲓ ⲉⲧⲛⲁⲛⲟⲩϥ ⲛⲛⲥⲟϭⲛ ⲙⲛⲛϣⲟⲩϩⲏⲛⲉ ϣⲁϥϣⲱⲡⲉ ϩⲛⲟⲩⲁⲡⲁⲧⲏ ·",
      "english": "Yet again in the case of the smell. If the nose be in the habit of taking delight in the things which have sweet smells, that is, in scented unguents, and in aromatic perfumes, and in balsams, it falleth at length into a state of numbness,",
      "source": "On Susanna",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:pschrysostom.susanna.budge:1-63",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲛⲁⲓⲥⲑⲏⲥⲓⲥ ⲇⲉ ⲛⲉ ⲡⲃⲁⲗ ⲉⲧⲉⲡⲛⲁⲩ ⲉⲃⲟⲗ ⲡⲉ · ⲙⲛⲡⲥⲱⲧⲙ ⲙⲛⲡ**ϣⲱⲗⲙ** ⲙⲛⲡϫⲓϯⲡⲉ · ⲙⲛⲡϭⲙϭⲟⲙ ⲉⲣϣⲁⲛⲧⲙⲗⲁⲁⲩ ϭⲉ ⲛⲁⲓⲥⲑⲏⲥⲓⲥ ⲡⲗⲁⲛⲁ · ⲏ ⲛⲥⲉⲧⲁⲕⲟ ·",
      "english": "Now the senses are the eye, that is to say, the sight, and the hearing, and the smelling, and the taste, and the touch ; and if the soul be not led astray by any one of these senses, or corrupted thereby,",
      "source": "On Susanna",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:pschrysostom.susanna.budge:1-63",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲛϩⲟⲥⲟⲛ ⲇⲉ ⲛϣⲁϫⲉ ⲙⲛⲛⲉⲛⲉⲣⲏⲩ ⲁⲓϣⲱⲗⲙ ⲉⲩⲥϯⲛⲟⲩϥⲉ ⲛⲟϭ ⲙⲡⲓ**ϣⲱⲗⲙ** ⲛⲧⲉϥϩⲉ · ⲉⲛⲉϩ ·",
      "english": "And whilst we were talking together I smelled a strong sweet smell, the like whereof I never smelled before.",
